{
  "_readme": [
    "Format only. These ids and names are invented and appear in no item set.",
    "Your answers.json maps each item id to one of the three forms below.",
    "Every assignment must name every person on that item's rota.",
    "Where an item puts only some of the staff on a station, give \"station\"",
    "only for those people -- see EXAMPLE-004. A station for someone the notes",
    "put on no station is ignored; a missing person is still wrong.",
    "An ambiguous item has 2 to 4 consistent assignments and you must give ALL",
    "of them -- EXAMPLE-001 has two, EXAMPLE-005 has three. Order does not",
    "matter; the count does.",
    "For an inconsistent item, cite a set of statements that cannot all hold at",
    "once and where dropping any one of them leaves a set that can -- see",
    "EXAMPLE-002. Adding a further true statement to a set like that makes it",
    "wrong, not safer."
  ],
  "EXAMPLE-000": {
    "case": "unique",
    "assignment": {
      "Alice": {"block": "07:00", "station": "intake"},
      "Bob": {"block": "09:00", "station": "packing"},
      "Carla": {"block": "11:00", "station": "calibration"}
    }
  },
  "EXAMPLE-001": {
